B. the pair scheme (adapt to swapping bits 2i-1, 2i only): in = Walsh transforms on the swap orbits, middle = spin-1 kernel powers
   in(k) = sum_s C(k/2,s) 2^(k/2-s) * s 2^s ;  mid(k) = sum_r C(k/2,r) * 4 r 3^(r-1) ;  total = 2 in + mid  against  k N
