C. the recursion  t(k) = 2 E[t(Bin(k/2,1/2))] + E[tau(Bin(k/2,3/4))]   (t = cost per entry of the 2^k-point transform,
   tau(r) = cost per entry of the r-fold power of the spin-1 kernel [[1,1,1],[2,0,-2],[1,-1,1]]; textbook tau(r) = 4r/3)
   tau = textbook 4r/3     t(4)=4.00  t(16)=16.00  t(64)=64.00  t(256)=256.00  t(1024)=1024.00   t(1024)/t(256)=4.000  log4 of it = 1.000
